{
  "source": "course-assets/training-bias/training-bias.mp4",
  "duration": 202.4533125,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.02,
      "end": 5.28,
      "text": "Computer vision researchers once encountered a problem that revealed a lot about how AI"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.28,
      "end": 5.74,
      "text": "learns."
    },
    {
      "start": 6.62,
      "end": 11.36,
      "text": "They trained a model that became highly accurate at recognizing cows in familiar photographs."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.06,
      "end": 16.54,
      "text": "But when they showed that exact same model of photo of a cow standing on a sandy beach,"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.0,
      "end": 21.16,
      "text": "its performance fell apart, it completely failed to recognize the animal."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.94,
      "end": 25.16,
      "text": "Most of the cows it learned from during training appeared on green pasture."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.0,
      "end": 27.04,
      "text": "The model picked up a shortcut."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.04,
      "end": 29.1,
      "text": "Green grass equals cow."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.76,
      "end": 33.0,
      "text": "It absorbed the background instead of identifying the actual animal."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.7,
      "end": 35.34,
      "text": "This is the core of training bias."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.08,
      "end": 38.48,
      "text": "Training data can create two distinct traps."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.1,
      "end": 44.28,
      "text": "It can be skewed, which creates a distorted picture of reality, or it can be stale, creating"
    },
    {
      "start": 44.28,
      "end": 44.96,
      "text": "an old picture."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.66,
      "end": 50.9,
      "text": "This diagram shows how skewed data distorts an AI's worldview through three overlapping"
    },
    {
      "start": 50.9,
      "end": 51.32,
      "text": "problems."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.94,
      "end": 53.0,
      "text": "The first is defaults."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.0,
      "end": 57.86,
      "text": "When common cases appear very frequently in the training data, the model starts to treat"
    },
    {
      "start": 57.86,
      "end": 60.54,
      "text": "them as the standard, universal answer for everything."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.24,
      "end": 62.32,
      "text": "The second is blind spots."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.96,
      "end": 67.04,
      "text": "Rare cases might barely appear in the data at all, so the model learns almost nothing"
    },
    {
      "start": 67.04,
      "end": 67.62,
      "text": "about them."
    },
    {
      "start": 68.18,
      "end": 69.3,
      "text": "The third is wrong patterns."
    },
    {
      "start": 70.02,
      "end": 74.0,
      "text": "If a secondary detail consistently predicts the right answer during training, the model"
    },
    {
      "start": 74.0,
      "end": 76.84,
      "text": "ignores the core concept and relies on that detail instead."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.58,
      "end": 79.34,
      "text": "These patterns carry heavy consequences."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.1,
      "end": 84.08,
      "text": "Demographic accuracy gaps in facial analysis systems have been documented by researchers,"
    },
    {
      "start": 84.74,
      "end": 87.56,
      "text": "and errors in face recognition have played a role in wrongful arrests."
    },
    {
      "start": 88.34,
      "end": 92.18,
      "text": "You cannot fact check your way out of this trap, because every individual piece of information"
    },
    {
      "start": 92.18,
      "end": 93.52,
      "text": "in the answer might be correct."
    },
    {
      "start": 94.1,
      "end": 95.68,
      "text": "Instead, you have to look for sameness."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.3,
      "end": 101.3,
      "text": "When every example looks alike, you are seeing the model's data default, not reality."
    },
    {
      "start": 102.2,
      "end": 106.9,
      "text": "To find what the first answer left out, you can use three specific questioning techniques"
    },
    {
      "start": 106.9,
      "end": 109.76,
      "text": "to force the AI to reveal the missing context."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.68,
      "end": 111.64,
      "text": "The first is direct."
    },
    {
      "start": 112.22,
      "end": 114.24,
      "text": "Ask, what's missing from this answer?"
    },
    {
      "start": 115.14,
      "end": 117.1,
      "text": "The second technique looks for outliers."
    },
    {
      "start": 117.48,
      "end": 121.6,
      "text": "Tell the AI, show me examples that don't fit the pattern you just gave."
    },
    {
      "start": 122.5,
      "end": 124.62,
      "text": "The third clears away common data points."
    },
    {
      "start": 125.18,
      "end": 128.5,
      "text": "Tell it, answer again, leaving out the most famous examples."
    },
    {
      "start": 129.42,
      "end": 132.84,
      "text": "The AI model typically does have the rest of the picture in its data."
    },
    {
      "start": 133.16,
      "end": 137.68,
      "text": "It simply won't lead with that information unless you prompt it to break its default pattern."
    },
    {
      "start": 138.5,
      "end": 140.48,
      "text": "Outdated data creates a different trap."
    },
    {
      "start": 141.1,
      "end": 142.68,
      "text": "AI training eventually stops."
    },
    {
      "start": 143.3,
      "end": 147.48,
      "text": "Anything happening in the real world after that cut-off date is missing from its worldview."
    },
    {
      "start": 148.4,
      "end": 151.52,
      "text": "An AI doesn't always have to rely strictly on its static training."
    },
    {
      "start": 152.14,
      "end": 156.96,
      "text": "It can look outside itself using a system called retrieval augmented generation, or REG."
    },
    {
      "start": 157.68,
      "end": 158.56,
      "text": "First is retrieve."
    },
    {
      "start": 158.56,
      "end": 163.08,
      "text": "The system actively searches for outside information connected to your prompt."
    },
    {
      "start": 163.74,
      "end": 165.08,
      "text": "Second is add to context."
    },
    {
      "start": 165.8,
      "end": 171.36,
      "text": "That newly retrieved material is joined with the active information the AI can use for this specific answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 171.9,
      "end": 175.3,
      "text": "Finally, the model uses that material to write its answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 175.88,
      "end": 180.7,
      "text": "This process does not update the model's original training data, or change its internal weights."
    },
    {
      "start": 181.28,
      "end": 185.44,
      "text": "It just places the material into the active context for this specific response."
    },
    {
      "start": 186.16,
      "end": 191.32,
      "text": "However, it does not guarantee the source is reliable, or that the AI will interpret it correctly."
    },
    {
      "start": 192.92,
      "end": 195.12,
      "text": "AI repeats the shape of its data."
    },
    {
      "start": 195.86,
      "end": 196.5,
      "text": "Ask what's missing."
    },
    {
      "start": 197.4,
      "end": 198.06,
      "text": "Check what's changed."
    }
  ],
